    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0254" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.94/1136.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-15T17:00:00+01:00">September 15,
                            1939—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 15—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1986. The Chinese Embassy in Paris informs us that Sun Fo called on Molotov
                    yesterday and requested information regarding the Soviet-Japanese negotiations
                    which he understood were being carried on.</p>
                <p>In reply Sun Fo received assurances that there would be no change in the Soviet
                    foreign policy vis-à-vis the Far East.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d227-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d227-f1" n="32" xml:id="d227-f1-content">
                <p>See also telegram No. 546 bis, September 15, midnight, from the Ambassador in the
                    Soviet Union, <ref target="#pg70">p. 70</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
